      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T02:01:51Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): the converter from a kernel plan to a toolpath\n\nAdd camcraft_motion::kernel_emit: emit_plan and emit_levels turn the\nkernel Plan of each level into a Toolpath in the plan's order. The\nconverter makes no decision of its own: it refuses a step that it cannot\nemit by name, never drops a step and never adds a cut. Lateral rapids\nonly at the clearance height; below the stock top only the moves of a\nproved step that starts where the tool stands. A lift is a retract to\nthe clearance height with its reason in the notes in the links.rs text.\nExact circles become G2/G3 arcs; leads and helices stay chords.\n\nThe K4 motion pin now builds the whole plan (with the entry and exit\nstage) and converts it with the real converter; its counts stay. A new\npin runs the camcraft-sim verifier on the converted disc and dog-bone\nplans. No old planner and no app code calls the converter yet.\n\nRefs #4269\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
